WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.351 --> 00:00:17.400
It turned out that Mickey was right about Coach's decision.

2
00:00:18.361 --> 00:00:21.644
As soon as Patrick arrived for the Hornets game, Coach hurried over.

3
00:00:21.664 --> 00:00:24.646
"Feeling better, Patrick?"

4
00:00:24.666 --> 00:00:26.708
"Yep." "Good.

5
00:00:26.968 --> 00:00:28.209
Because you're starting today."

6
00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:30.891
Mickey flashed Patrick a grin.

7
00:00:30.911 --> 00:00:31.952
"I knew it."

8
00:00:32.916 --> 00:00:35.738
"Thanks. We'll see how it goes," Patrick said.

9
00:00:36.959 --> 00:00:41.362
Mickey was probably disappointed, but he wasn't showing it, not at all.

10
00:00:42.423 --> 00:00:44.624
Patrick had studied the Hornets players carefully.

11
00:00:45.224 --> 00:00:51.068
So the game went well—until the fifth inning when the Hornets scored a run, and the Dragons couldn't

12
00:00:51.088 --> 00:00:51.549
catch up.

13
00:00:52.409 --> 00:00:55.391
At the top of the seventh inning, the Hornets were still leading.

14
00:00:56.272 --> 00:01:00.275
The first two Dragons batters got on base, but the next two struck out.

15
00:01:00.875 --> 00:01:01.856
Gene was up next.

16
00:01:03.264 --> 00:01:06.767
"Gene's a great baseman but a weak hitter," Patrick thought.

17
00:01:07.347 --> 00:01:08.348
Coach waved to Mickey.

18
00:01:09.469 --> 00:01:11.151
"Here it comes," Patrick thought.

19
00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:13.432
"Time to put Mickey in as pinch hitter."

20
00:01:13.452 --> 00:01:15.414
"Mickey," said Coach.

21
00:01:15.434 --> 00:01:16.975
"Go in to hit for Gene."

22
00:01:17.976 --> 00:01:19.077
Gene handed off the bat.

23
00:01:19.097 --> 00:01:20.778
"You got this, Mickey."

24
00:01:21.719 --> 00:01:23.601
"Oh well," Patrick told himself.

25
00:01:23.621 --> 00:01:26.983
"I won't get to finish the game, but at least I started."

26
00:01:27.944 --> 00:01:30.426
Still Patrick knew that Coach had made the right call.

27
00:01:31.407 --> 00:01:34.745
The team needed a hit, and Mickey was the player most likely to get one.

28
00:01:34.765 --> 00:01:37.406
"Come on, Mickey," Patrick said.

29
00:01:37.426 --> 00:01:38.746
"Get a hit!"

30
00:01:41.287 --> 00:01:43.047
Mickey popped a foul on the first swing.

31
00:01:43.828 --> 00:01:47.429
Patrick could see Mickey digging deep, fiercely eyeing the pitcher.

32
00:01:48.629 --> 00:01:52.010
The second pitch was fast and outside, just like Mickey liked them.

33
00:01:54.531 --> 00:01:57.532
He slammed the ball far into center field and took off.

34
00:01:58.548 --> 00:02:02.531
The crowd roared as the first and then the second Dragons runner crossed home.

35
00:02:03.272 --> 00:02:04.513
Mickey slid into third.

36
00:02:04.533 --> 00:02:07.536
"Safe!" cried the umpire.

37
00:02:08.376 --> 00:02:09.597
The score was 2-1.

38
00:02:10.858 --> 00:02:13.801
Buck struck out, and now the Hornets were up to bat.

39
00:02:14.802 --> 00:02:18.264
Patrick pushed his way over to Mickey as the team started to take the field.

40
00:02:18.284 --> 00:02:20.826
"Nice hit, Mickey.

41
00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:23.268
You were patient at the plate, and it paid off.

42
00:02:23.869 --> 00:02:26.211
The pitcher—" "Hey, Patrick!"

43
00:02:26.671 --> 00:02:27.312
It was Daniel.

44
00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:28.601
"Dell's waiting!"

45
00:02:28.621 --> 00:02:31.622
"Huh?" What was Daniel talking about?

46
00:02:32.182 --> 00:02:33.643
Mickey was taking over as catcher.

47
00:02:35.204 --> 00:02:37.185
Daniel grinned at Patrick's confused look.

48
00:02:37.885 --> 00:02:39.306
"Mickey's going to third base.

49
00:02:39.766 --> 00:02:40.907
You're catching for Dell.

50
00:02:41.868 --> 00:02:44.169
Coach doesn't want to mess up the rhythm you two have going."

51
00:02:44.949 --> 00:02:47.771
Patrick nodded and quickly buckled on his catching equipment.

52
00:02:51.012 --> 00:02:54.094
His nerves were thrumming—he couldn't make a mistake now.

53
00:02:55.075 --> 00:02:56.375
One run would tie the game.

54
00:02:56.816 --> 00:02:59.293
Two runs would cost the Dragons the game.

55
00:03:00.173 --> 00:03:04.955
Patrick squatted and swept the field with his eyes, making sure his teammates were all in position.

56
00:03:07.176 --> 00:03:08.677
The batter stepped into the box.

57
00:03:09.337 --> 00:03:10.837
Patrick signaled for a curve.

58
00:03:11.498 --> 00:03:16.080
Dell threw the strikes: one, two, three, batter out!

59
00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:18.741
The second batter had a choppy swing.

60
00:03:20.681 --> 00:03:22.362
He popped a foul on the first pitch.

61
00:03:24.903 --> 00:03:26.664
Patrick signaled for a changeup next.

62
00:03:27.392 --> 00:03:28.313
Dell threw the ball.

63
00:03:30.334 --> 00:03:35.578
"Strike!" Patrick settled into position and signaled for a fastball next.

64
00:03:36.399 --> 00:03:37.720
Dell threw the pitch high.

65
00:03:40.221 --> 00:03:42.243
The batter popped it out toward left field.

66
00:03:42.903 --> 00:03:46.746
Todd took off after the foul and caught it, smacking hard into the fence.

67
00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:49.388
"Two outs!"

68
00:03:49.708 --> 00:03:50.349
thought Patrick.

69
00:03:50.369 --> 00:03:51.990
"One more for the win!"

70
00:03:53.011 --> 00:03:54.652
Suddenly the crowd moaned.

71
00:03:57.284 --> 00:04:00.445
Patrick glanced up and saw Todd clutching his left shoulder.

72
00:04:01.386 --> 00:04:04.507
Coach met him on the field and then walked him back to the dugout.

73
00:04:04.527 --> 00:04:10.890
"Oh no," thought Patrick, exchanging glances with Dell.

74
00:04:11.470 --> 00:04:13.691
The two of them had just about wrapped up this game.

75
00:04:14.631 --> 00:04:19.713
Coach looked from player to player, his forehead wrinkled as he tried to decide what to do.

76
00:04:20.794 --> 00:04:22.514
Finally he made a decision.

77
00:04:22.534 --> 00:04:26.256
"Patrick, I think you and Dell can finish this.

78
00:04:26.976 --> 00:04:30.117
I'll send Pete to third base and Mickey into left field."

79
00:04:31.598 --> 00:04:33.759
Patrick reached down and rubbed his lucky mitt.

80
00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:37.160
Things were finally going his way.

81
00:04:38.241 --> 00:04:40.682
Then he looked at the next batter and groaned.

82
00:04:42.903 --> 00:04:45.864
Number 28 was a power hitter who tended to pull left.

83
00:04:46.664 --> 00:04:49.205
The Dragons had to have a strong fielder in left field.

84
00:04:49.886 --> 00:04:52.046
He thought for only a second before speaking up.

85
00:04:52.066 --> 00:04:55.568
"Coach?" Everyone was looking at Patrick.

86
00:04:56.588 --> 00:04:59.069
"This next guy is a power hitter, and he pulls left.

87
00:04:59.769 --> 00:05:04.311
So Patrick paused, suddenly nervous about questioning Coach's decision.

88
00:05:04.331 --> 00:05:07.453
"So I was thinking about our positions.

89
00:05:08.173 --> 00:05:11.854
Mickey can catch well, but I'd probably be better in left field."

90
00:05:12.655 --> 00:05:13.395
Coach frowned.

91
00:05:13.415 --> 00:05:15.856
"You sure about the batter's hitting, Patrick?"

92
00:05:16.656 --> 00:05:17.337
Patrick nodded.

93
00:05:17.357 --> 00:05:19.497
"I know the Hornets' batters pretty well."

94
00:05:19.517 --> 00:05:22.259
"Then good call," Coach said.

95
00:05:22.939 --> 00:05:23.699
He looked at Mickey.

96
00:05:23.719 --> 00:05:24.780
"Suit up.

97
00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:25.580
You're catching."

98
00:05:26.444 --> 00:05:27.745
Patrick unbuckled his gear.

99
00:05:27.765 --> 00:05:32.589
"Come on, Mickey," said Dell.

100
00:05:33.069 --> 00:05:34.010
"Let's finish this."

101
00:05:37.253 --> 00:05:40.075
As Mickey headed toward home plate, Patrick grabbed his sleeve.

102
00:05:40.095 --> 00:05:43.237
"I'd go with the changeup and a high pitch."

103
00:05:44.398 --> 00:05:45.019
Mickey nodded.

104
00:05:45.039 --> 00:05:50.824
"Thanks." Patrick trotted out to left field, hoping he hadn't steered Mickey or Coach wrong.

105
00:05:53.145 --> 00:05:56.088
He stood ready, but the batter fouled the first two pitches.

106
00:05:57.192 --> 00:05:59.414
"Hang in there, Dell," thought Patrick.

107
00:05:59.434 --> 00:06:01.415
"One more pitch could do it."

108
00:06:02.496 --> 00:06:04.017
But the next pitch was wild.

109
00:06:05.398 --> 00:06:08.019
Mickey dove to block the ball and made the recovery.

110
00:06:10.261 --> 00:06:11.822
The next two pitches were balls.

111
00:06:12.542 --> 00:06:16.465
Now there was a full count: the batter had two strikes and three balls.

112
00:06:17.426 --> 00:06:18.666
Patrick's heart pounded.

113
00:06:20.588 --> 00:06:21.188
This was it.

114
00:06:21.929 --> 00:06:23.870
The Dragons could win with this next play.

115
00:06:24.830 --> 00:06:26.872
But Patrick could see that Dell was tired.

116
00:06:27.828 --> 00:06:32.572
"Fastball!" Patrick thought, wishing there was some way to communicate his thought to Mickey.

117
00:06:33.353 --> 00:06:38.837
From experience, Patrick knew that Dell could throw a fastball straight down the slot, no matter how tired

118
00:06:38.877 --> 00:06:39.258
he was.

119
00:06:40.679 --> 00:06:43.381
Dell wound up and zipped the ball toward the catcher's mitt.

120
00:06:44.662 --> 00:06:47.124
The batter swung, and the ball popped straight up.

121
00:06:48.986 --> 00:06:51.708
Mickey scrambled to pull off his mask as the crowd roared.

122
00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:55.371
Patrick screamed with the rest of them.

123
00:06:55.391 --> 00:06:56.392
"Catch it!"

124
00:06:57.256 --> 00:07:00.738
Mickey spotted the ball as it sailed down toward a spot behind home plate.

125
00:07:01.778 --> 00:07:03.179
He turned and took off running.

126
00:07:04.839 --> 00:07:06.680
He dived under the ball and rolled.

127
00:07:08.661 --> 00:07:10.782
Patrick squeezed his eyes shut for a second.

128
00:07:11.442 --> 00:07:12.963
Would Mickey come up with the ball?

129
00:07:13.943 --> 00:07:16.344
Mickey raised his mitt from a cloud of dust.

130
00:07:16.364 --> 00:07:19.685
"Out!" cried the umpire.

131
00:07:19.705 --> 00:07:22.847
"Woo-hoo!" shouted Patrick.

132
00:07:23.527 --> 00:07:25.368
The Dragons had beaten the Hornets!

133
00:07:27.116 --> 00:07:28.897
The other players mobbed Mickey.

134
00:07:31.539 --> 00:07:32.899
Patrick ran in to join them.

135
00:07:35.221 --> 00:07:37.442
"Smart thinking today, Patrick," Coach said.

136
00:07:37.462 --> 00:07:40.844
"We're lucky to have someone who can play well in two positions.

137
00:07:42.145 --> 00:07:45.487
And maybe someday we'll have another Deboe coaching too!"

138
00:07:46.627 --> 00:07:47.908
Daniel gave him a fist bump.

139
00:07:47.928 --> 00:07:50.029
"Proud of you, bro."

140
00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:54.292
Patrick grinned as he went back onto the field to shake hands with the Hornets.

141
00:07:55.284 --> 00:07:59.487
Crouching behind home plate and catching pitches was one of the greatest feelings he knew.

142
00:07:59.507 --> 00:08:05.332
"But the best thing about playing baseball," he thought, "is being part of a team."
